Wait — crearProcesarOutbox takes outboxRepository/notificacionRepository directly (pool-bound), good for worker. But in tests I wanted procesarOutbox wired after commit. In test helper, InMemory repos work directly too — no transaction needed for the worker (it's post-commit). But should the worker be transactional? RF-024/RNF-017: notification failure must not invalidate reservation. Non-transactional per-event processing is correct.Hmm — one design flaw: notificacion insert + markProcesado not atomic — if notificacion succeeds but markProcesado fails, duplicate notification on retry. For academic scale acceptable; note in report. Could wrap in uow: crearProcesarOutbox({ejecutarTransaccion}) — better! Use uow with fn(repos) per event:

```js
export function crearProcesarOutbox({ ejecutarTransaccion, reloj }) {
  return async function procesarOutbox() {
    const pendientes = await ejecutarTransaccion({}, (r) => r.outbox.findPendientes(50));
    for (const evento of pendientes) {
      try {
        await ejecutarTransaccion({}, async (r) => {
          const carga = JSON.parse(evento.carga);
          await r.notificaciones.insert({...});
          await r.outbox.markProcesado(evento.id, ...);
        });
        procesados++;
      } catch ...
    }
  };
}
```
This gives atomicity per event. Let me rewrite to take ejecutarTransaccion — consistent with the rest.

