parts.text:
Two bugs:

1. `citas-router.js` is at `adapters/http/` → domain is at `../../domain/cita.js` (up http→adapters→reservas, then domain). I wrote `../domain/cita.js` — wrong. Fix: `../../domain/cita.js`. Also check `parseIdParam` import in citas-router: `../../../../shared/http/params.js` — from adapters/http → 4 ups → src ✓ correct. And params.js ValidationError import: `../../../shared/http/errors.js` — params.js is at src/shared/http/ → `../../../` = codigo root/shared... WRONG! src/shared/http/params.js → to reach src/shared/http/errors.js should be `./errors.js`. Let me check params.js: I wrote `import { ValidationError } from '../../../shared/http/errors.js';` — from src/shared/http: .. → shared, ../.. → src, ../../.. → codigo → codigo/shared/http/errors.js — DOESN'T EXIST. Fix to './errors.js'.

2. Disponibilidad: full-day exception NOT blocking. Look at excepcionAfecta:
```js
function excepcionAfecta(excepcion, dia, inicioMin, finMin) {
  if (excepcion.fecha !== dia) return false;
```
WAIT — `dia` is the weekday name ('lun'), but `excepcion.fecha` is '2026-11-16'! The function compares fecha (YYYY-MM-DD) against dia (weekday)! This is the bug — written in the earlier session. It should compare `excepcion.fecha !== fecha` where fecha is the date string. The caller: `excepcionAfecta(e, dia, iniMin, finMin)` passes `dia` (weekday). Fix: pass fecha (the date) instead of dia:

```js
function excepcionAfecta(excepcion, fecha, inicioMin, finMin) {
  if (excepcion.fecha !== fecha) return false;
  ...
}
...
if (excepciones.some((e) => excepcionAfecta(e, fecha, iniMin, finMin))) return false;
```

