Line 159: `invalida` — profesional tries Confirmada → Atendida, expected 409 TRANSICION_NO_PERMITIDA but got 403. In cambiarEstado:

```js
const esAdmin = actor.rol === 'administrador';
const esProfesionalAsignado = actor.rol === 'profesional' && cita.profesional_id === actor.id;
```

cita.profesional_id = 1, actor.id = 3 (the profesional's USUARIO id, not the profesional id!). The profesional row id is 1, usuario_id is 3. The cita stores profesional_id = 1 (the profesional entity id). But req.sesion.usuarioId = 3. So `cita.profesional_id === actor.id` → 1 === 3 → false → 403!

This is a **real domain modeling issue**: the cita.profesional_id FK references profesional.id, while sessions carry usuario.id. For ownership checks (puedeModificarCita too — same bug! `if (rol === 'profesional') return cita.profesional_id === usuarioId` — WRONG), we must map usuario → profesional id.

In the main test, reprogramar/cancelar by solicitante worked (solicitante_id === usuarioId ✓ same entity). Professional ownership needs the mapping.

Fix strategy: in cambiarEstado (and puedeModificarCita professional branch), resolve the profesional row for actor: `const perfil = await repos.profesionales.findByUsuarioId(actor.id)` then compare `cita.profesional_id === perfil.id`. Update puedeModificarCita signature? It's a pure domain function taking (rol, usuarioId, cita) — for profesional it should compare against profesional_id of the ACTOR, not usuarioId. Cleanest: change puedeModificarCita to accept `actor = { rol, usuarioId, profesionalId }` where profesionalId is resolved by the caller. Or keep domain pure and resolve in use cases:

In exigirEligibilidad / cambiarEstado use cases, before ownership check, if actor.rol === 'profesional': `const perfil = await repos.profesionales.findByUsuarioId(actor.id); const actorProfesionalId = perfil?.id ?? null;` and call `puedeModificarCita(actor.rol, actor.id, cita, actorProfesionalId)`.

Update domain puedeModificarCita:
```js
export function puedeModificarCita(rol, usuarioId, cita, profesionalId = null) {
  if (rol === 'administrador') return true;
  if (rol === 'solicitante') return cita.solicitante_id === usuarioId;
  if (rol === 'profesional') return profesionalId !== null && cita.profesional_id === profesionalId;
  return false;
}
```

And in cambiarEstado:
```js
const perfil = actor.rol === 'profesional' ? await repos.profesionales.findByUsuarioId(actor.id) : null;
const esProfesionalAsignado = actor.rol === 'profesional' && perfil && cita.profesional_id === perfil.id;
```

In exigirEligibilidad (async context? it's sync currently — receives cita/actor). Make it async and fetch perfil inside via repos, or resolve before calling. exigirEligibilidad is called from reprogramar/cancelar which have repos — pass repos and make exigirEligibilidad async:

```js
async function exigirEligibilidad({ repos, cita, actor, ahora, minAnticipacion, justificacion, esReprogramacion }) {
  const perfil = actor.rol === 'profesional' ? await repos.profesionales.findByUsuarioId(actor.id) : null;
  const actorProfesionalId = perfil?.id ?? null;
  if (!puedeModificarCita(actor.rol, actor.id, cita, actorProfesionalId)) throw 403...
```

Also update the unit test for puedeModificarCita — it tests profesional: puedeModificarCita('profesional', 20, cita) with cita.profesional_id=20 — with new signature needs profesionalId param: puedeModificarCita('profesional', 3, cita, 20). Update unit test.

Also the professionnel GET /citas list uses actor.id vs profesional filter — listarCitas for professional filters by profesionalId: actor.id — SAME BUG: professional usuario id 3 vs profesional id 1. Fix: resolve perfil in listarCitas:

```js
if (actor.rol === 'profesional') {
  const perfil = await repos.profesionales.findByUsuarioId(actor.id);
  if (!perfil) throw403;
  const filtro = filtroProfesional !== null && Number(filtroProfesional) !== perfil.id ? throw : perfil.id;
  citas = findAll({..., profesionalId: perfil.id})
}
```

Main test asserted `profeLista.body.every(c => c.profesional_id === 1)` — with the bug, findAll({profesionalId: 3}) returns [] — every() on empty = true → passed vacuously! Fix makes it actually filter correctly.

Apply the fixes.

